---
title: "Stata help file"
description: >
  The help file of the Stata command, as displayed by `help bootmakr`.
---

```{r helpers, include = FALSE}
source(file.path(getOption("bootmakr.precompute.dir"), "helpers.R"))
```

This is the help file that `help bootmakr` opens in Stata, converted to
plain text. For a guided introduction see
[Get started in Stata](stata.html); for the corresponding R arguments see
[R and Stata side by side](r-and-stata.html).

```{r, echo = FALSE, results = "asis"}
f <- file.path(.pc_dir(), "stata", "output", "bootmakr-help.txt")
txt <- readLines(f, warn = FALSE, encoding = "UTF-8")

# Drop the Stata logo above the title and the common left margin.
txt <- txt[grep("^\\s*Title\\s*$", txt)[1]:length(txt)]
txt <- sub("\\s+$", "", txt)
margin <- min(nchar(sub("^( *).*$", "\\1", txt[nzchar(txt)])))
txt <- substring(txt, margin + 1)

cat("```{.stata-help}", txt, "```", sep = "\n")
```
